# Slipstream keeper configuration. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
# These bots run continuously on a VM (NOT serverless) and crank the protocol.

# --- RPC endpoints ---
BASE_RPC=https://api.devnet.solana.com
ER_RPC=https://devnet.magicblock.app

# --- Operator / keeper signing key ---
# Path to the Solana keypair JSON the keepers sign with. On the VM, place the
# file somewhere safe (chmod 600) and point this at it. NEVER commit this file.
KEEPER_KEYPAIR=/home/slipstream/.config/solana/id.json

# --- Deploy manifest ---
# Path to deploy.json (live on-chain addresses). Defaults to the repo-root copy.
DEPLOY_MANIFEST=/app/deploy.json

# --- Optional overrides (defaults are fine for the live devnet deployment) ---
# USDC_MINT=Fakb9gPACMBbfQgepdAEmPCYmNU4iKAqQhFKfrDU6gDr
# USDC_VAULT=BTWVG5oDmomaMkpdX4xYgfjr1gpEGodW5oPe3k5P71qr
# PYTH_FEED=7UVimffxr9ow1uXYxsr4LHAcV58mLzhmwaeKvJ1pjLiE

# --- Fill-log settlement keeper ---
# FILL_LOG_START_EPOCH=0
#
# Fills indexer DB (keepers/data/fills.db, read by the frontend's /api/trades
# and /api/status) grows unbounded by default — nothing ever deletes a row.
# Set this to opt into pruning fills older than N days (checked at most
# once/day):
# INDEXER_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# --- Market-maker / taker bots (demo liquidity; optional) ---
# BOT_MM_COUNT=2
# BOT_TAKER_COUNT=2
#
# On the current live devnet deployment, the DEFAULT bot wallet names (mm-0,
# mm-1, taker-0, taker-1) are stuck: their TradingCredits are half-delegated
# (L1 says delegated, so fund_trading_credit refuses; the ER never actually
# took ownership, so the delegation program refuses to undelegate either). A
# TradingCredit PDA derives from the owner keypair, so a fresh name is the
# only way out. docker-compose.yml and ecosystem.config.js (pm2) both already
# set these; if you're running bots any other way (a bare `npm run bots`, a
# custom script), set them too or every bot order will silently fail:
# BOT_MM_PREFIX=mm-v2
# BOT_TAKER_PREFIX=taker-v2
